      "data": {
        "text": "DONE -- merged as PR #319 (merge commit 8d24fbf; branch commits 72a3d55 + 091a446, merged main d631903).\n\nROOT CAUSE. The boss-approach term (card b56633fb) was correctly calibrated against the FIRE GATE; the defect was one level down, in what 'gun range' meant. DoAIFire gated on the CENTRE distance to the target -- the 2008 test verbatim (src_decompiled/EvilAliens/PlayerShip.cs:549) -- and the approach anchor is derived from that same test on purpose, so the ship parked where its centre distance equalled the bullet's travel and threw the target's whole hull away. Measured before: boss=159px edge on ?level=Level2&marsboss against a 176px corner term, and r*=118px on BrainBoss against a 351px reach.\n\nTHE FIX. A bullet only has to reach the HULL. PlayerShip.AiGunReachPx = bullet travel + the target's hull radius -- one rule, no per-type code, shared by the fire gate and the anchor so they cannot drift. The credit is the INSCRIBED half-extent (ThreatRadius), not the sqrt(2) corner term: conservative on an axis approach, and self-limiting against the aim spread. r*: MarsBoss 175 -> ~300px, BrainBoss 118 -> ~276px.\n\nMEASURED (DIRECTIONAL, N=32 = seeds 1-8 x2 -- NOT the N=60 bar), eahl, Very_Hard, no ?invuln, 300s, paired against ?aigunhull=0 (the pre-card gate):\n  brainboss  deaths 3.12 vs 5.44 (+2.31 +- 0.38, outside 2 SEM)  boss= 189 vs 109px  bossfar 0.9% vs 27.4%  idle 0.6% vs 15.0%\n  marsboss   deaths 11.50 vs 12.00 (n.s.)  boss= 168 vs 161px  bossfar 0.9% vs 20.0%  idle 0.8% vs 17.2%  win@155s vs 181s\nLevel 1 and the spider rig flat within SEM at N=16; killers=SpiderBoss(standing) did NOT rise.\n\nA SHIPPED INVARIANT WAS RESTATED, deliberately -- read before 'fixing' it. Pushing r* outward moves most configurations into the branch where the boss's own repellent has decayed below the whole-sum floor, so the solved weight floors at 0.2 and a live powerup detour out-votes the boss. Where the repellent IS audible at r* nothing changed (crossing exact, out-vote holds). Where it is not, the bot fetches the pickup from a safe standoff and returns, and what keeps the level advancing is the X > 2000 sentinel -- extracted as PlayerShip.ChooseBossSteerTarget so logic_probe verifies the TAKEOVER rather than restating the floor (mutation-tested: dropping the sentinel fails that leg and only that leg). Clamping the vote is NOT available: steerTargetWeight IS the pull magnitude, so a clamp moves the equilibrium back inward and reintroduces the solved-constant-plus-discontinuity b56633fb designed out.\n\nNEW SEAM: ?aigunhull=<0..1> scales the credit; 0 restores the pre-card gate AND anchor exactly. A tuning knob, not a bug reproduction, so it is OUT of DebugFlags.Active (the ?aisweptmax= precedent). New row in logic_probe's ?ai* rejection table.\n\nALSO: marsboss added to tools/sim/ai_sweep.py's RIGS presets. The exponent damping is now inert at every shipped configuration and its comment says so loudly -- it is the BOUND, not dead code.\n\nFOLLOW-UP FILED: card 5c89e4e6 -- DoAIFire does not LEAD its target, which matters more now that bullet flight times roughly doubled.\n\nGATES: logic_probe 0 failures, 60/60 headless probes, clean Debug build (all re-run after merging main, which brought T1's fix/ai-edge-repel-powerups in). No Chrome pass -- AI steering is headless-verifiable end to end, agreed with the overseer. The N=60 scoring gate is a later pass and was deliberately NOT run here.",
